From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: vote the GPU's memory bandwidth

The SM8450 GPU node has no interconnect path and its OPPs no bandwidth,
unlike SM8550's. The A730 has no GMU bandwidth table in the driver, so its
DDR vote comes from dev_pm_opp_set_opp() on the "gfx-mem" path, and with
none the GPU's traffic reached DDR only through the LLCC bandwidth
monitor's reaction. Once the interconnects' sync_state dropped the boot
votes, the AYANEO Pocket VERT's games ran at the GPU's top OPP and stopped
around 90 fps where they had reached 120.

Add the path as SM8550 has it and a peak vote per OPP: the stock tree's bus
level for the nearest stock GPU frequency at or above it. At 818 MHz the
GPU now votes 13.1 GB/s, DDR follows to its top step, and Horizon Chase
reaches 120 fps again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
@@ -2455,6 +2455,10 @@
 			iommus = <&adreno_smmu 0 0x400>,
 				 <&adreno_smmu 1 0x400>;
 
+			interconnects = <&gem_noc MASTER_GFX3D QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
+					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
+			interconnect-names = "gfx-mem";
+
 			operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 
 			qcom,gmu = <&gmu>;
@@ -2472,61 +2476,73 @@
 				opp-818000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <818000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <13085937>;
 				};
 
 				opp-791000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <791000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <13085937>;
 				};
 
 				opp-734000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <734000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <12484375>;
 				};
 
 				opp-640000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <640000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_SVS_L2>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
 				};
 
 				opp-599000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <599000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_SVS_L1>;
